// **The case that produces NaN**, driven through the whole simulation rather
// than through one unit test.
//
// Five bodies at exactly the same point. There is no line between them to push
// along, so normalising their difference is a division by zero — and a NaN
// position is not merely wrong, it is wrong in a way that reads as success:
// `clamp` does not recover it, and it compares `false` to everything, so the
// usual `if off > tolerance` shape of a positional assertion *passes*. The
// runner's unconditional finiteness check is what actually catches it; these
// assertions on top say the cluster resolved sensibly rather than merely
// remaining numeric.
//
// It is not a contrived case. A crowd converging on one target arrives at one
// point, which is exactly what the seek behaviour will produce.
//
// Measured: the cluster settles on tick 15, and the trace records the whole
// descent — ten pairs in contact on tick 0, then five, then four while the line
// straightens out, then nothing. The budget is 60 so that "and then it stays
// settled" is part of what the golden file asserts.
//
// The tolerances below are **bounds, not precisions** — the deliberate
// exception to the rule that a wide tolerance is an assertion switched off.
// What is being asserted is that the cluster did not detonate: after settling,
// every body is still within a body's-length or so of where it started. The
// golden trace is what pins the exact behaviour, tick by tick, including how
// many pairs were in contact on each one.
//
// Away from the origin so the player, which is not moving, is never involved.
(
    description: "Five bodies at one point fan out to a stable ring instead of NaN.",
    setup: (
        actions: [
            Place((20.0, 0.0)),
            Place((20.0, 0.0)),
            Place((20.0, 0.0)),
            Place((20.0, 0.0)),
            Place((20.0, 0.0)),
        ],
    ),
    inputs: [],
    budget: (ticks: 60),
    expect: (
        contacts: 0,
        crowd_contacts: 0,
        enemy_count: 5,
        bodies: [
            (nth: 0, alive: true, pos: (x: 20.0, z: 0.0, tol: 1.5)),
            (nth: 1, alive: true, pos: (x: 20.0, z: 0.0, tol: 1.5)),
            (nth: 2, alive: true, pos: (x: 20.0, z: 0.0, tol: 1.5)),
            (nth: 3, alive: true, pos: (x: 20.0, z: 0.0, tol: 1.5)),
            (nth: 4, alive: true, pos: (x: 20.0, z: 0.0, tol: 1.5)),
        ],
        trace: "a_coincident_cluster_fans_out.trace",
    ),
)
